---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import AppShell from '../components/AppShell.astro';
import IndexCard from '../components/IndexCard.astro';
import DeskThings from '../components/DeskThings.astro';
import { PAPER } from '../lib/paper';
// TODO(Abishek): read the note below in your own voice and rewrite anything that isn't you.
---

<Base title="Notes · Abishek R Edakkalathur" description="About Abishek, and how this site was made." tint="#EDB54A" statusInk={PAPER.fg}>
  <Fragment slot="left"><IndexCard compact /></Fragment>

  <AppShell slug="notes" theme={PAPER} label="Notes">
    <p class="date">Notes · Kochi</p>
    <h1>hi,</h1>
    <p>I'm Abishek, an independent developer from Kerala.</p>
    <p>
      I build apps around how people here actually live: bank SMS and UPI, Malayalam, a sports hall with bad wifi, ten friends
      splitting one dinner bill. Most of them work offline, keep your data on your phone, and come with more tests than they
      strictly need.
    </p>
    <p>Everything on this phone is something I designed and built myself, except Dazzle Designs, which I made for a client.</p>

    <h2>How this site was made</h2>
    <p>
      It's an Astro site pretending to be a phone. Each app opens in its own colours and fonts, taken from the real app. The
      clock is Kochi time, and after 7 pm the wallpaper goes lamp-lit.
    </p>
    <p>On a phone there's no frame: the page is the home screen. Pull an app down to close it.</p>
    <p>And if you press and hold any icon on the home screen, you'll find out I couldn't resist.</p>
  </AppShell>

  <Fragment slot="right"><DeskThings thing="pen" /></Fragment>
</Base>

<style>
  .date {
    margin: 4px 0 0;
    font: 400 11.5px/1 var(--mono);
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--app-muted);
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 18px 0 14px;
    font: italic 400 64px/0.9 var(--serif);
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 32px 0 10px;
    font: 400 28px/1.05 var(--serif);
  }
  p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.62;
  }
</style>
